- op: create  # 375f
  at: '2026-06-20T19:50:43Z'  # 375f
  by: agent  # 375f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 375f
  clock: 1  # 375f
  nonce: 375f  # 375f
  data:  # 375f
    kind: work_item  # 375f
    title: "test_check_schema_coverage._BaselineSwap races on the shared real baseline file under pytest -n auto"  # 375f
    status: todo_soft  # 375f
    priority: 3  # 375f
    parent:  # 375f
    tags:  # 375f
    - ci_infrastructure  # 375f
    isbefore: []  # 375f
    duplicate_of: []  # 375f
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 375f
    pr_ref:  # 375f
    description: "Pre-existing parallel-isolation flake (surfaced 2026-06-20 during INV-loguk closure). packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_check_schema_coverage.py uses a _BaselineSwap context manager + _run_gate subprocess that read/write/delete the SHARED real repo file .ci/schema-coverage-baseline.json (the gate script reads a fixed path, so tests mutate the real file in place and restore on exit). Under pytest -n auto (the smart-test default), concurrent xdist workers running different _BaselineSwap contexts race on that single file — one test does _BaselineSwap(None) which DELETES it while another expects its written baseline — producing spurious gate exit-1 (observed: TestSchemaConformanceFold::test_baseline_tolerated_violation_warning_mode_passes failing with 'corpus output has 1 nodes / 1 edges; assert 1==0'). Passes cleanly in isolation and serially (verified: 97 passed serial). Risk: spurious CI failures on any PR touching symbol_kinds.py / the gate (pulls these tests into the affected set). Fix options: (a) add a baseline-path override to scripts/check-schema-coverage (env var e.g. HYPERGUMBO_SCHEMA_BASELINE or a --baseline flag) and have _BaselineSwap/_run_gate point at a per-worker tmp file via tmp_path instead of mutating the repo file; or (b) mark the affected tests no-xdist (serial group). Option (a) is the structural fix. scripts/check-schema-coverage is NOT a governance file."  # 375f
    fields: {}  # 375f
- op: discuss  # d4fd
  at: '2026-09-19T04:31:46Z'  # d4fd
  by: agent  # d4fd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d4fd
  clock: 2  # d4fd
  nonce: d4fd  # d4fd
  message: "REPRODUCED 2026-09-19 during WI-binis's chunked slice (smart-test -n 4 on a 42-file chunk containing this file): 4 of 12 tests fail, a different 4 each run (test_update_baseline_writes_sorted_dedup, test_newly_covered_value_passes_with_hint, test_baseline_tolerated_violation_warning_mode_passes, test_new_uncovered_value_fails on the second run), all green under -n 1, and the race LEAVES .ci/schema-coverage-baseline.json modified in the working tree (+54/-2) — a tracked file, so the next `git add` of .ci/ would commit a test's scratch baseline. Running the file alone under -n 4 reproduces it without any other test present, so it is this file's own tests racing each other, not cross-file. Mitigation used today: run the file serially and `git checkout -- .ci/schema-coverage-baseline.json`. Suggest the fix already implied by the row: give the gate a --baseline PATH flag (or HYPERGUMBO_TEST_BASELINE env) so the tests never touch the real file."  # d4fd
